SUMMARY:2424 Finch Avenue West
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T203000
UID:1427@haveyoursay.toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Project: City Planning & Development Review Community Consulta
 tion Meetings\n\nThe City of Toronto’s Development Review Division has r
 eceived an Official Plan and Zoning By-law Amendment application to redeve
 lop a site that is designated as 'General Employment Areas' on Map 13 of t
 he City of Toronto's Official Plan and Employment Heavy Industrial (EH 1.0
 ) and Industrial-Commercial (MC) under the former North York Zoning By-law
  7625. The proposal contemplates nine new mixed-use buildings\, including 
 residential and non-residential uses. The proposal includes a new public s
 treet right-of-way with two new intersections located on Finch Avenue West
  and Milvan Drive. The proposal includes a new 3\,267 square metre public 
 park located at the northeast portion of the site.\n\nType: In person
LOCATION:Gord and Irene Risk Community Recreation Centre\, 2650 Finch Ave 
 W\, North York\, ON\, Canada
URL:https://haveyoursay.toronto.ca/city-planning-development-review-commun
 ity-consultations/2424-finch-avenue-west
X-SOURCE:City Planning Consultations
END:VEVENT
